## Conventions
- Follow standard Go conventions (gofmt -l ., go vet ./..., go tool staticcheck ./...)
- All public API functions should have doc comments
- Error handling: wrap errors with context using fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)
- Prefer table-driven tests with descriptive sub-test names
- Use internal/ visibility to keep the public surface minimal
- Thread-safety: document lock ordering; prefer sync.RWMutex for shared state

## Agent struct (internal/agent)
Agent is the per-session god-object; keep it from regrowing.
- New per-session state belongs in an embedded domain group (sessionPersist, sessionStats, compactionState, backgroundState, featureWiring, subagentWiring, toolRegistry, turnCounters, sessionMeta) defined in the matching domain file — not a flat field on Agent. Field promotion keeps a.field access unchanged.
- New feature tools wire through SessionAgentOptions / NewSessionAgent (the factory) and are gated by the single featureTools() policy in tool_registry.go; avoid adding ad-hoc Set* construction-time setters.
- Keep agent.go to the Agent struct, NewAgent, and genuinely cross-cutting methods. Domain methods live in their domain files (turn.go, compaction.go, session.go, subagent.go, …).
- When moving a field, move its concurrency comment with it — the statsMu / persistMu leaf-lock notes are the safety contract.
